{"author":{"id":"7674679dac9170669f752d932f8b5955b1d55717359e13b1c1e687003c7bb99f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790009546,"nonce":"00kUBbMixdoheRrjwdE01fNuET4=","title":"Task: Automation rules: trigger, condition, action over the op log","message":"The engine. A rule is trigger + condition + action, evaluated over operations rather than over snapshots, so 'status changed to X' is expressible rather than merely 'status is X'.\n\n- Triggers: an op of a kind (SetField on a given field, AddRelation of a type, comment added, issue created), an iteration boundary, or a schedule.\n- Conditions: the query language (3c9c24d), evaluated against the issue's snapshot after the op.\n- Actions: set a field, add or remove a relation, comment, transition, assign. All expressed as ordinary ops written by the rule's author identity, so the op log shows what fired and why.\n\nForced by the runtime decision (221b629): actions are idempotent, and progress is a watermark over the op log rather than a per-rule done-flag, because more than one evaluator may fire for the same change and ops arrive eventually.\n\n8573d99 (flow pr) is a hardcoded instance of one rule; it should become a shipped default rule rather than parallel code.","files":null},{"type":9,"timestamp":1790009546,"nonce":"02jdVqe0x2paA+3RpoSNVihP34U=","key":"type","value":"task"},{"type":9,"timestamp":1790009546,"nonce":"t4kDJNHzEU7SM2U3m/1RueWZSx4=","key":"status","value":"to-do"}]}